The audience is first-time, never-licensed Vermont applicants, typically teenagers on the learner's permit and junior license path and adults applying for a first driver's license, reading at a plain-English level with no assumed driving vocabulary. This section teaches how to handle oncoming glare, how to enter and leave an interstate through acceleration and deceleration lanes, the interstate safety rules including stopping, lane use, fatigue, missed exits and the stopped emergency vehicle rule, the wrong way warning, and when and how to pass on the left or right. The content assumes no prior rule knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy; every term the section introduces is defined in the glossary lines of part C.
